# xfig draw-line smoke test - synthesize a click on the line drawing
# tool followed by two clicks on the canvas, asserting that the canvas
# region picks up a non-zero changed pixel ratio. Drives the GXxor
# rubber-band feedback path and the canvas backing pixmap XCopyArea
# flow that libx11-compat is most likely to regress.
#
# Coordinates assume the default xfig toolbox layout against the
# XFIG_SMOKE_GEOMETRY value baked into mk/xfig.mk. The button-1 click
# on (32, 96) targets the "line" tool icon; the two canvas clicks at
# (480, 320) and (640, 480) walk a diagonal line endpoint pair.
delay 3000
wait-window "Xfig|xfig" 8000
delay 2000
screenshot initial
motion 32 96
button 1 click
delay 500
motion 480 320
button 1 click
delay 200
motion 640 480
button 1 click
delay 500
screenshot drawn
assert-image drawn common-visible.json
assert-image drawn xfig-canvas-changed.json
